Odoo 20 Community listens on port 8069. Configuration is
/etc/odoo/odoo.conf. Data and filestore live in /var/lib/odoo.

1. Create the database role. Odoo creates databases itself, so the
   role needs CREATEDB:

   su - postgres -c "createuser -d -R -S odoo"
   systemctl enable --now postgresql

2. Set admin_passwd in /etc/odoo/odoo.conf. That password protects
   database create/drop/backup on the web manager, not a company login.

3. Start the service and open http://localhost:8069 :

   systemctl enable --now odoo

The first page asks for a database name, a master password (the
admin_passwd above), and the first user of that database.
